./expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/23-l2-pin1-design/codex/fidelity-review-pivotframe-answer.md:6:The proof sets `Qt = fromBlocks VJ⁻¹ (-(VJ⁻¹ * VK)) 0 1`, then `Q = reindex e.symm e.symm Qt`. It proves `reindex e e Q = Qt`, rewrites with `Matrix.toBlocks_fromBlocks₂₂`, and gets `isUnit_one`; see [lines 169-187](/home/ubuntu/workspace/geometry-of-dln-fibre/lean/DLNFibre/DLN/RLCT/Validate/DeepestPivotFrame.lean:169). So yes: the `₂₂` block is literally the bottom-right block of `fromBlocks`, in the pivot split.
./expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/23-l2-pin1-design/codex/fidelity-review-pivotframe-answer.md:8:The unit claim for `Q` is also sound: `Qt` is block upper triangular with unit diagonal blocks, and reindexing by equivalences preserves `IsUnit`; see [lines 173-181](/home/ubuntu/workspace/geometry-of-dln-fibre/lean/DLNFibre/DLN/RLCT/Validate/DeepestPivotFrame.lean:173).
